---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../../components/PageHead.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../data/site';
---

<Base title="Terms of use" description="The terms for using the Lumo desktop app and the Lumo website.">
  <PageHead eyebrow="Legal" title="Terms of use">
    <p class="legal-meta">Last updated 16 October 2026 · Pre-release draft</p>
  </PageHead>
  <div class="container prose">
    <div class="lu-callout" data-tone="warning" role="note">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M8 2 1.5 13.5h13L8 2Z"></path><path d="M8 6.5v3M8 11.5h.01"></path></svg>
      <div>
        <div class="lu-callout-title">Draft for the pre-release period</div>
        <div>These terms will be reviewed and may change before the first release. Changes will be posted on this page with a new date.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 id="software">The software</h2>
    <p>
      Lumo is a desktop application that runs on your computer. It is provided “as is”, without warranty of any kind, to the
      extent permitted by law. Pre-release builds may contain bugs, change without notice, or lose data; keep backups of anything important,
      especially in folders you grant to Lumo.
    </p>

    <h2 id="your-responsibility">Your responsibility for actions</h2>
    <p>
      Lumo proposes and carries out actions on your behalf, but only within the permissions you grant and with the approvals it asks you for. You
      are responsible for reviewing approvals and confirmations before you accept them, and for what you ask Lumo to do. Do not use Lumo for
      anything unlawful or to violate the rights or terms of others.
    </p>

    <h2 id="providers">Model providers and third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      Lumo connects to services you choose, such as accounts you link, and links you to others, such as delivery apps and merchants. Your use of
      those services is governed by their own terms and privacy policies, and you pay them directly. Lumo is not a party to orders or purchases you
      make with them, does not process payments, and is not affiliated with or endorsed by them unless stated.
    </p>

    <h2 id="output">AI output</h2>
    <p>
      Answers and content produced with AI models can be wrong or incomplete. Lumo checks the results of its own actions where it can, but check
      anything that matters, such as prices, opening hours, dates and facts, before relying on it.
    </p>

    <h2 id="website">This website</h2>
    <p>
      The content of this website describes software that is still being built. Features marked “In development” or “Planned” are not available
      and may change or not ship.
    </p>

    <h2 id="liability">Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the maximum extent permitted by law, the Lumo contributors are not liable for any indirect, incidental or consequential damages, or for
      loss of data, arising from your use of Lumo or this website.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about these terms can be raised as a <a href={SITE.issues}>GitHub issue</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
